{"title":"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f7cf27c522dbcdf92907b546e9ed1ca69f75c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD^{}_{}$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> below has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f55b6221d0aec91e18c8c6de3688a43f447c102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{}_{} = 12 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dff5a0aec6ae9cc6ef52cbe7579067e42e1762c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^{}_{} = 13 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">Diagonals</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddf51f143406f1270d64001fa85b8f77d4f4c41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P^{}_{}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.  If triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a562065eec19251aa9cb52dc22d89cc051960f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABP^{}_{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" /> is cut out and removed, edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41699a79262163c0df579406c575f506f6dfb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bb1db3d066da48df7576e30ef3831ec64cecc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BP}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> are joined, and the figure is then creased along segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10459c41998a2ef73e2f7296c658de55c89ac8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70cabfec7d6a77caf8fa94bdaaf883751f489242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DP}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, we obtain a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangular_pyramid&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Triangular pyramid (page does not exist)\">triangular pyramid</a>, all four of whose faces are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangles</a>.  Find the volume of this pyramid.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1000e30e6f2569a527b722be1df0f5760223056a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair D=origin, A=(13,0), B=(13,12), C=(0,12), P=(6.5, 6); draw(B--C--P--D--C^^D--A); filldraw(A--P--B--cycle, gray, black); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, N); label(&quot;$13\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, A--D, S); label(&quot;$12\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, A--B, E);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"212\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1(Synthetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1(Synthetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1.28Synthetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1(Synthetic)\">Solution 1(Synthetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1(Synthetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1cbcb7495cc0c1c813d23912314dfdbc69406e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; pointpen = black;  pathpen = black+linewidth(0.7);  pen small = fontsize(9); currentprojection = perspective(20,-20,12); triple O=(0,0,0); triple A=(0, 399^(0.5), 0); triple D=(108^(0.5), 0, 0); triple C=(-108^(0.5), 0, 0); triple Pa; pair Ci=circumcenter((A.x,A.y),(C.x,C.y),(D.x,D.y)); triple P=(Ci.x, Ci.y, (99/133)^.5);  Pa=(P.x,P.y,0);  draw(P--Pa--A); draw(C--Pa--D);  draw((C+D)/2--A--C--D--P--C--P--A--D); label(&quot;A&quot;, A, NE); label(&quot;P&quot;, P, N); label(&quot;C&quot;, C); label(&quot;D&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;$13\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (A+D)/2, E, small); label(&quot;$13\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (A+C)/2, N, small); label(&quot;$12\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (C+D)/2, SW, small); [/asy]\" width=\"658\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>Our triangular pyramid has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9c3edb72e93e39c3d757ff64d770cfa6eafe2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt{3} - 13\\sqrt{3} - 13\\sqrt{3} \\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />. The area of this isosceles triangle is easy to find by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb680abb362aa56ced52a57c0a0d2bac1bd16bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ACD] = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" />, where we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d235a79d5532dc1a5be2233138bbf6f7ce7c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{ACD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06afce734fadc63b3063995d46cc8e2539883686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{399}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab1d1d437ce9c4a9fbba80ccf3ac31d3d7cc6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac 12(12\\sqrt{3})\\sqrt{399} = 18\\sqrt{133}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"237\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0542b2fd08bce2046cb8d05182b09ec35535e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(280); import three;  pointpen = black;  pathpen = black+linewidth(0.7);  pen small = fontsize(9); real h=169/2*(3/133)^.5;  currentprojection = perspective(20,-20,12); triple O=(0,0,0); triple A=(0,399^.5,0); triple D=(108^.5,0,0);  triple C=(-108^.5,0,0); pair Ci=circumcenter((A.x,A.y),(C.x,C.y),(D.x,D.y)); triple P=(Ci.x, Ci.y, 99/133^.5); triple Pa=(P.x,P.y,0); draw(A--C--D--P--C--P--A--D); draw(P--Pa--A); draw(C--Pa--D); draw(circle(Pa, h)); label(&quot;A&quot;, A, NE); label(&quot;C&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;D&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;P&quot;,P , N); label(&quot;P$&#39;$&quot;, Pa, SW); label(&quot;$13\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (A+D)/2, E, small); label(&quot;$13\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (A+C)/2, NW, small); label(&quot;$12\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, (C+D)/2, SW, small); label(&quot;h&quot;, (P + Pa)/2, W); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}$&quot;, (C+P)/2 ,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"462\" height=\"285\" /> \n</p><p>To find the volume, we want to use the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0ee4de8561ebbcab1988ceb2c3bf5e69963b3372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 13Bh = 6\\sqrt{133}h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />, so we need to find the height of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tetrahedron\" title=\"Tetrahedron\">tetrahedron</a>. By the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb3725ae9268d15da9f91be6b041f5efb4cba14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = CP = DP = \\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"41\" />. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sphere\" title=\"Sphere\">sphere</a> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f3e0560d2e1ef7616e3790583d3fedb585fd04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"41\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0121b8b8997401226b4f8b07aab9d5d65d704d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> lie on the sphere. The cross section of the sphere that contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/0121b8b8997401226b4f8b07aab9d5d65d704d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is a circle, and the center of that circle is the foot of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> from the center of the sphere. Hence the foot of the height we want to find occurs at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>From here we just need to perform some brutish calculations. Using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5a879852fe3c6fe76a5c30164a22d4b1992e34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 18\\sqrt{133} = \\frac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumradius\" title=\"Circumradius\">circumradius</a>), we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399ad8d1b4818640b40b72db828eae5d93dedb10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac{12\\sqrt{3} \\cdot (13\\sqrt{3})^2}{4\\cdot 18\\sqrt{133}} = \\frac{13^2\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{133}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"240\" height=\"45\" /> (there are slightly <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">simpler ways</a> to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> since we have an isosceles triangle). By the Pythagorean Theorem, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf5a8ceec0f81611b43efc0388da1a3c47ded5ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}h^2 &amp;= PA^2 - R^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{13^2\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{133}}\\right)^2\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{939 \\cdot 133 - 13^4 \\cdot 3}{4 \\cdot 133} = \\frac{13068 \\cdot 3}{4 \\cdot 133} = \\frac{99^2}{133}\\\\ h &amp;= \\frac{99}{\\sqrt{133}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"332\" height=\"177\" />\n</p><p>Finally, we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> into the volume equation to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be6c4e19bb387940d9a860a989873d6cb91aed98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = 6\\sqrt{133}\\left(\\frac{99}{\\sqrt{133}}\\right) = \\boxed{594}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> (or the triangle with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4092f2eed412f468c2fa111b4e4d23bb9796b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328017b7be493264f1a6df6c88ad54423eb248af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328017b7be493264f1a6df6c88ad54423eb248af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />) be the base of our tetrahedron. We set points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/b/57b0a6f5992d7990de8cf0ecdb98fd078a4a5aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6\\sqrt {3}, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c5f63c0a73f20fe2e5e434ce03a3342bf786d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$( - 6\\sqrt {3}, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"21\" />, respectively. Using Pythagoras, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a4f42a47f87d641f266df25e856d4989778b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\sqrt {399}, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" />. We know that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> of the tetrahedron (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) has to be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitude</a> of the tetrahedron. Since the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04ac66bf3ce35cbcecee08328cfea8f1a1e696b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sqrt {939}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"41\" />, we can write three equations using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula\" title=\"Distance formula\">distance formula</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c78cba2c39d65b2fbae619793df66388087a9ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^{2} + (y - \\sqrt {399})^{2} + z^{2} &amp;= \\frac {939}{4}\\\\ (x - 6\\sqrt {3})^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} &amp;= \\frac {939}{4}\\\\ (x + 6\\sqrt {3})^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} &amp;= \\frac {939}{4} \\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"124\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the last two equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f51d57011f1c7cc6b8e9035808e3936ce524817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" /> with a bit of effort, we eventually get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f609045f3d20a79d3341b4ca244f5f624625bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac {291}{2\\sqrt {399}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"88\" height=\"42\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7304c98f9c51ff73a95219baa2c18aa5e01fb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\frac {99}{\\sqrt {133}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"78\" height=\"42\" />.\nSince the area of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b2e29f35bfb1de5d06ce87682bd5a8437912ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{2}\\cdot bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />, we have the base area as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e913e4bbd57c8100869588ca0c670c98961a3533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18\\sqrt {133}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da0b32c7bdf3a71d7f3afcee6ed5992ab7846c0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = \\frac {1}{3}\\cdot18\\sqrt {133}\\cdot\\frac {99}{\\sqrt {133}} = 6\\cdot99 = 594$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"301\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the apex of the pyramid and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. We find the side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f04bd1a6e57dbf4b77bfe16cb2a9f28ea2c6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XMP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930629ae38067e5e8d6481bf84f5cf3c80bda87f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MP = \\frac{13\\sqrt3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is half of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5637d15c5593faee076f798e555fa81b9eafeb56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3\\cdot13^2+3\\cdot12^2}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"210\" height=\"43\" />. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8950f5281116064aaff1b97e61a3a498c5264d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, consider right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f17ebffa5186c47cbdd2fd7e683410e68626b8a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XMD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />; since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/46298c43039ae435450f7df27d158d8fa7d24a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XD=13\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/9895447c74958ab62340ce6efe950ebe6d17b370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=6\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d80adb1cd9709e9608cfde5f4f1e24e66c92d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX=\\sqrt{3\\cdot13^2-3\\cdot6^2} = \\sqrt{399}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"253\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b23c17487efebb5f8f49659e4ee15b06207c082a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\angle XPM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />. For calculating trig, let us double all sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f04bd1a6e57dbf4b77bfe16cb2a9f28ea2c6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XMP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. By Law of Cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e448524f2d36c0f693516e6ada1794b82fc8342f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{3\\cdot13^2+939-4\\cdot399}{2\\cdot13\\cdot3\\sqrt{313}}=\\frac{-150}{6\\cdot13\\sqrt{313}}=-\\frac{25}{13\\sqrt{313}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"450\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8106c068311c88a8c0c211957cfb0836784e2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\theta = \\sqrt{1-\\cos^2\\theta}\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de6afccbadd0e8c74761dcc37c1fd952e14e41c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{625}{13^2\\cdot313}}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/8080dbc86a651923c15d4d5e2d0533c85647cb40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{\\sqrt{13^2\\cdot313-625}}{13\\sqrt{313}}\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a383645a559e41d69723d9e64ef9f834bad133.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{\\sqrt{3\\cdot132^2}}{13\\sqrt{313}}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa17ca7c9d1a977072e09a0c0e4413ef1900435d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{132\\sqrt3}{13\\sqrt{313}}\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"45\" />\nThus, the height of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9309f0bc03ccb0531b2d79909baea8355982eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX\\sin\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt{939}}{2}\\cdot\\frac{132\\sqrt3}{13\\sqrt{313}}=\\frac{66\\cdot3}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"287\" height=\"48\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee30a4f958546811e9291b2dac359309fbff27c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CPD]=3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot13\\sqrt{3}=9\\cdot13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"234\" height=\"24\" />, the volume of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59e387947aa4583d3a406e603702a797a251f087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13 \\cdot 9\\cdot13\\cdot \\frac{66\\cdot3}{13}=\\boxed{594}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME\" title=\"1990 AIME\">1990 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1990 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1990\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1990 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 2